+# Changes
+
+## Round 0
+
+- `src/kv.mjs`: added `parseKeyValue(text)`, the inverse of `renderKeyValue`.
+  Skips blank and `#` comment lines, splits on the first `=` only, trims the
+  key, keeps the value verbatim (surrounding whitespace, quotes and `#` are
+  all part of the value), lets a later duplicate key win, accepts CRLF, and
+  throws `SyntaxError` (with the line number) on a line with no `=` or an
+  empty key, `TypeError` on non-string input. Uses `Object.defineProperty` so
+  a `__proto__` key becomes an own property instead of changing the prototype.
+- `tests/kv.test.mjs`: 15 new tests, one per rule above plus a
+  `parseKeyValue(renderKeyValue(o))` round-trip over several objects.
+- `README.md`: documents `parseKeyValue` with an example and one sentence per
+  edge, and notes that round-trip holds for keys without surrounding
+  whitespace and string values without newlines.
