+# Review: parseKeyValue (loop `review`, round 0)
+
+## Ship line, item by item
+
+1. `npm test` passes — HOLDS. `.grooph/parse-key-value/runs/20260920-191110/round-0.npm-test.txt:22-25` reports 17 tests, 17 pass, 0 fail; re-run by the critic gives the same (17/17).
+2. Skips blank lines and `#` comment lines — HOLDS. `src/kv.mjs:32-33` trims the line and `continue`s on empty or `#`-leading text; tested at `tests/kv.test.mjs:24-26` with an empty line, a whitespace-only line, a `# db` line and an indented comment.
+3. A value may contain `=`; only the first `=` splits — HOLDS. `src/kv.mjs:34` uses `indexOf("=")`, `src/kv.mjs:38` takes the rest verbatim; tested at `tests/kv.test.mjs:28-33` with `sslmode=require` and `a=b=c`.
+4. `parseKeyValue(renderKeyValue(o))` gives back `o` for plain string values without newlines — HOLDS. Tested at `tests/kv.test.mjs:80-90` over `{}`, an ordinary object, values containing `=`, `#`, quotes, padding and the empty string, and a non-sorted key order. The value side of the promise is met; see aspiration finding 1 for keys.
+5. README.md documents `parseKeyValue` with one example — HOLDS. `README.md:12-13` shows a call and its result; `README.md:22-43` is the section.
+
+## Aspiration findings, ranked
+
+1. `README.md:26-28` states the round-trip precondition as "keys have no surrounding whitespace", which is too weak: a reader predicting from the README alone would expect `{ "#x": "y" }`, `{ "a=b": "c" }` and `{ "": "x" }` to round-trip, and they do not (probed: `{}`, `{ a: "b=c" }`, `SyntaxError` respectively, because `src/kv.mjs:33` treats the rendered `#x=y` as a comment, `src/kv.mjs:34` splits `a=b=c` at the first `=`, and `src/kv.mjs:37` rejects `=x`). None of these key shapes is in the round-trip test at `tests/kv.test.mjs:81-86`. State the full precondition in one sentence (key is non-empty, contains no `=`, and does not start with `#` after trimming) and add one negative case to the test.
+2. `README.md:41` decides CRLF but not a `\r` anywhere else: `src/kv.mjs:31` drops only a `\r` at the end of a line, so `a=1\rb=2\r` gives `{ a: "1\rb=2" }` (probed) and a value ending in `\r` loses it on round-trip (`{ a: "x\r" }` -> `{ a: "x" }`, probed). Neither is tested (`tests/kv.test.mjs:56-58` covers CRLF only). One sentence ("a lone `\r` is not a line break; a `\r` before `\n` is dropped, even inside a value") and one assertion would close it.
+3. `README.md:31` says "first non-space character is `#`", but `src/kv.mjs:32` uses `trim()`, so a tab-indented `#` is also a comment (probed: `\t#c\na=1\n` -> `{ a: "1" }`). Say "non-whitespace" to match, and add a tab to the case at `tests/kv.test.mjs:25`, which uses spaces only.
+
+All seven edges named in the aspiration (whitespace around keys `README.md:33`, around values `README.md:34`, duplicate key `README.md:37`, quoted value `README.md:35`, no `=` `README.md:38`, empty key `README.md:39`, trailing comment `README.md:36`, CRLF `README.md:41`) are decided, stated in one sentence each, and tested (`tests/kv.test.mjs:35-67`). The remaining distance to the aspiration is the three items above.
+
+## Verdict
+
+verdict: pass
diff --git a/src/kv.mjs b/src/kv.mjs
index 937965b..da699a0 100644
--- a/src/kv.mjs
+++ b/src/kv.mjs
@@ -12,3 +12,32 @@ export function renderKeyValue(object) {
   }
   return out;
 }
+
+/**
+ * The inverse of `renderKeyValue`: one property per `key=value` line of
+ * `text`, in line order. Blank lines and lines whose first non-space
+ * character is `#` are skipped. Only the first `=` splits a line; the key is
+ * trimmed, the value is taken verbatim (spaces, quotes and `#` included).
+ * A later duplicate key overwrites an earlier one. A line with no `=` or
+ * with an empty key throws a `SyntaxError` naming the line number.
+ * @param {string} text
+ * @returns {Record<string, string>}
+ */
+export function parseKeyValue(text) {
+  if (typeof text !== "string") throw new TypeError("parseKeyValue: string required");
+  const result = {};
+  const lines = text.split("\n");
+  for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {
+    const line = lines[i].endsWith("\r") ? lines[i].slice(0, -1) : lines[i];
+    const trimmed = line.trim();
+    if (trimmed === "" || trimmed.startsWith("#")) continue;
+    const eq = line.indexOf("=");
+    if (eq === -1) throw new SyntaxError(`parseKeyValue: line ${i + 1} has no "="`);
+    const key = line.slice(0, eq).trim();
+    if (key === "") throw new SyntaxError(`parseKeyValue: line ${i + 1} has an empty key`);
+    const value = line.slice(eq + 1);
+    // defineProperty so a key such as `__proto__` becomes an own property.
+    Object.defineProperty(result, key, { value, enumerable: true, writable: true, configurable: true });
+  }
+  return result;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kv.test.mjs b/tests/kv.test.mjs
